agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** The 0.3.46 DoR/TDD hardening adds a Step 5 obligation to map spec Validation Notes negative scenarios and treat missing negative coverage as a blocking gap, but the sole numeric Advance score still comes from `ac_ledger.cjs`, which initializes rows only from `- ACn:` lines (`criteriaFromSpec`) and never ingests Validation Notes entries. An agent can document negative-test gaps in prose, run `ac_ledger.cjs score`, receive ≥ `minVerifyScore` on AC coverage alone, and the orchestrator will Advance to Step 6 with no fail-closed hook for uncovered negative scenarios—undermining the new TDD contract this release introduces.

**Correção sugerida:**

```javascript
// ac_ledger.cjs — parse Validation Notes bullets and fail-closed when uncovered
function negativeScenariosFromSpec(text) {
  const notes = text.match(/## Validation & Observation Notes[\s\S]*?(?=\n## |$)/i)?.[0] || '';
  return [...notes.matchAll(/^[-*]\s+(.+)$/gm)]
    .map((m) => m[1].trim())
    .filter(Boolean);
}

// In init(): ledger.negativeScenarios = negativeScenariosFromSpec(specText).map(...)
// In scoreLedger(): if any negativeScenarios lack linked tests with phase 'observed', set missingNegative = true and score = Math.min(score, 8)
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 7/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: `ws-verify-plan/SKILL.md` L44–46 requires negative scenario mapping; L48 mandates `ac_ledger.cjs score` as the only score. `ac_ledger.cjs` L50–51 `criteriaFromSpec` regex-matches only `AC` lines; L84–96 builds ledger rows exclusively from those criteria. `ws-write-spec/SKILL.md` places negative scenarios under `## Validation & Observation Notes`, separable from ACs. 2. Scenario: Spec lists negative cases only in Validation Notes (not duplicated as ACs); implementation ships happy-path tests; verify step records gaps in the report but ledger scores 10/10; orch Step 5 gate passes at default 9 without negative tests ever being written. 3. Protection: `test/test-spec-dor-tdd.js` asserts skill prose contains “negative test” wording only; `test/test-validate-spec.js` covers authoring validation, not ledger/score integration; no test binds Validation Notes rows into `ac-ledger.json`. 4. Discards: Assuming interview/implement-tasks always catch missing red tests — those steps are advisory; Step 5 is the formal scored gate and explicitly disallows overriding the ledger score.

**Caminhos analisados:** /.agents/skills/ws-verify-plan/SKILL.md, /.agents/skills/ws-spec-to-pr/scripts/ac_ledger.cjs, /.agents/skills/ws-write-spec/SKILL.md, /.agents/skills/ws-implement-tasks/SKILL.md, /test/test-spec-dor-tdd.js
</details>

